# oracle: pair_style meam, single-element hcp reference (Ti of FeTiClibrary.meam, nn2(1,1) = 1, w47mn_ti.meam, zbl 0, Cmin(1,1,1) = 1, Cmax(1,1,1) = 1.44), non-periodic dimers at 2.2, 2.5, 2.7, 2.92, 3.2, 3.5, 3.8, 4.2 and 4.5 A (one clear/run 0 block per distance)
# oracle: the hcp 2NN shell enters the pair term through the reference structure; the dimer energies are native values (black box): -1.84730458099145, -2.39157544625346, -2.45472709420057, -2.38541715171305, -2.17757451094947, -1.86490900513837, -1.51903398500094, -1.10709245104215, -0.863837835051403 eV
# oracle-potentials: FeTiClibrary.meam
# oracle-inputs: w47mn_ti.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-6 abs=1e-9
clear
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        f f f
region          box block -40 40 -40 40 -40 40
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 single 0 0 0 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.2 0 0 units box
mass            1 47.88
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * FeTiClibrary.meam Ti w47mn_ti.meam Ti
thermo_style    custom step pe
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
